  "evidence": "TEXT_E: \"Get Brexit done\" and \"take back control of laws, borders, money and trade policy\"; oppose a second Scottish referendum; maintain defence spending above 2% and keep Trident; 20,000 more police, tougher sentencing, more prison places; record NHS cash boost with 50,000 more nurses, 6,000 GPs, mental health at parity; cross‑party social care reform and more support for carers; raise National Living Wage to two‑thirds of median; levelling up via UK Shared Prosperity Fund; end rough sleeping; build at least a million homes; controlled, points‑based immigration prioritising skills and contribution. TEXT_C: Green New Deal with £100bn+/yr investment; NHS +£6bn/yr, end fuel poverty, right to food, UBI, rent controls and end no‑fault evictions; remain and reform the EU with freedom of movement; halve the prison population, end the war on drugs, dismantle the hostile environment; cancel Trident and end arms sales; strong nature/animal agenda (Clean Air Act, ecocide law, end factory farming/hunting, rewilding, 700m trees).",
  "reasoning": "The electorate’s profile weights Care, Loyalty, Authority, and Equality while placing low emphasis on Sanctity; TEXT_E combines strong Loyalty/Authority cues (Brexit, Union, policing, defence) with substantial Care and some Equality (NHS boost, levelling up, living wage) and minimal Sanctity. TEXT_C excels on Care and Equality but runs counter to Loyalty/Authority (EU remain, demilitarisation, decriminalisation) and leans heavily on Sanctity/purity themes, making it less aligned overall.",
  "confidence": "medium",
  "winner": "TEXT_E"
